If we add $x^{2}$ to $f(x)$, we get the quadratic trinomial $(a+1) x^{2}+b x+c$, for which the maximum value is $-\frac{b^{2}}{4 a+4}+c$. If we subtract $4 x^{2}$ from $f(x)$, we get the quadratic trinomial $(a-4) x^{2}+b x+c$, for which the maximum value is $-\frac{b^{2}}{4 a-16}+c$. From this, we get the equations

$$
