We verify that for both values of $a$ the number $k$ is a natural number $(a=-18.5 \Rightarrow k=195$; $a=19.5 \Rightarrow k=233)$, so both values of $a$ are suitable.

4) The number $a$ lies to the right, and $a^{2}$ to the left of the segment $[k ; k+19]$. Obviously, this case does not fit, because if $a>a^{2}$, then both numbers $a$ and $a^{2}$ lie on the segment $[0 ; 1]$, but then there cannot be any integer between them.

