\end{array} \quad \Leftrightarrow x=5 ;\right.\right. \\
& \sqrt{x+4}-\sqrt{6-x}=-3 \Leftrightarrow \sqrt{x+4}+3=\sqrt{6-x} \Leftrightarrow\left\{\begin{array}{l}
x+4+6 \sqrt{x+4}+9=6-x, \\
